\section{Baseline Models}

\subsection{Binary Classification: Normal vs.\ Suspect}

A Logistic Regression model was first trained to classify connections as Normal or Suspect. When using all extracted features, including \texttt{ip} and \texttt{user}, the model achieved extremely high accuracy. However, a closer inspection of these results revealed feature leakage: some usernames and IPs appear exclusively in one class, making prediction artificially easy. Removing these features produced more realistic performance metrics.

