        \caption{Without user and ip}
    \end{subfigure}
    \caption{Effect of removing user/ip leakage.}
\end{figure}

Once identity-based features were removed, the Logistic Regression achieved approximately 96.5\% accuracy. The confusion matrix shows that misclassifications occur mainly in borderline cases where behavioural patterns overlap between normal and malicious activity.

\subsection{Failure Type Classification}

A Linear SVM was trained to predict \texttt{FailureType}. Similarly to the previous task, removing the \texttt{user} variable improved the fairness of evaluation by eliminating leakage.

