\section{Conclusion}

This project highlights the entire pipeline from log preprocessing to machine learning evaluation. The main limitation of the dataset is its low feature dimensionality: even after engineering new variables, only a small set of features truly drives the classification. As a result, models achieve very high accuracy with little effort.

The heatmap confirmed that the features are not redundant.  
The PCA showed that classes are naturally separable.  
The decision tree provided a clear explanation of the model’s behaviour.  
Random Forest and Gradient Boosting demonstrated that complex models do not improve the performance.

After these analyses, it became evident that retraining additional models would not lead to meaningful gains. The dataset’s structure, not the algorithms, is the limiting factor. Future work should therefore focus on richer feature extraction (session duration, geographic origin, sequence models, temporal patterns) rather than on trying new classifiers.


